{
 "encounter_id": "00755",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "It's this cough. Dry. Since I started the new blood pressure tablet."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Which tablet is that?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Ramipril. 5 mg. Once a day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "When did you start it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Three months ago."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Describe the cough."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Tickly. Dry. Worse at night. Nothing comes up."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any fever, or breathlessness, or wheeze? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. Just the tickle. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you smoke?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Never have."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any allergies to medicines?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Aspirin. I wheeze."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Anything else in your medical history?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "High blood pressure. That's it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check your pulse and oxygen. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Go on. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 70, oxygen 98 percent, blood pressure 130 over 80.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "All fine. I'll listen to your chest.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Clear? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Clear as a bell. No wheeze, no crackles. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "So it's the tablet? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "A dry, tickly cough that started a few weeks after ramipril, with a clear chest, is the classic pattern, so I can't rule out a cough caused by the ramipril."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Can you change it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Yes, there's an almost identical type of tablet, called losartan, that doesn't cause the cough. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Same effect? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Same blood pressure control. I'd like you to stop the ramipril and start losartan 50 mg once a day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. Today? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Today. Take the first one tomorrow morning, and don't take both."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "The cough can take a few weeks to fade after stopping, so don't expect it to vanish overnight. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "How long? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Up to four weeks. If it hasn't gone after four weeks, come back and I'll think again."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fair. Thanks. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Take care. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Bye. ~"
  }
 ],
